      "Language": "por",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 47 year-old man, with signals of low cardiac output due to sustained ventricular tachycardia, without history of pain. After clinical control of the arrhythmia, he was underwent to coronary-angiography that showed no obstructive lesion, but a thrombus was present in the distal right coronary artery. There was hypocinesia of the inferior wall of the left ventricle and the presence of a mural thrombus in that region. The patient was kept under clinical treatment and sent back to his cardiologist."},
